{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaRmJtWck5cnzMzyzKcB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `plus_eq_add` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\nThe proof uses induction on `m`:\n\n```lean\ntheorem plus_eq_add (n m : Nat) : plus n m = n + m := by\n  induction m with\n  | zero => rfl\n  | succ m ih => simp [plus, ih, Nat.add_assoc]\n```\n\n- **Base case (`m = 0`):** `plus n 0` reduces to `n` by definition, and `n + 0` also reduces to `n`, so `rfl` closes it.\n- **Inductive step (`m + 1`):** expanding `plus` gives `plus n m + 1`. The induction hypothesis turns that into `n + m + 1`, and `Nat.add_assoc` rewrites it as `n + (m + 1)`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":7857,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":441},"output_tokens":282,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf56034a-d1ff-4aae-9db3-2d901b7b451b","uuid":"d862fa75-5259-4216-9631-832bd8994eeb","timestamp":"2026-10-31T13:54:16.290Z","request_id":"req_011CgaRmJfs5NJnFyh1LsEwP"}
